-- statement:
--   **The three extra hypotheses of `P14NeedH'` hold at round-six parameters for large `n`.**
--   (1) is stated for every `N < 2^(6b)` (the caller's `vol·r + w + Ew D` is below that).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL3Hyps`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL3.p14_hyps_r6 (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) (K₀ : ℕ) : ∃ n₁ : ℕ, ∀ n, n₁ ≤ n →
--       Good P n ∧ 6 ≤ KP6 P n ∧
--       (∀ N : ℕ, N < 2 ^ (6 * bP6 n) → zsz (N : ℤ) ≤ pP6 P n) ∧
--       (pP6 P n + K₀) ^ 5 ≤ 2 ^ KP6 P n ∧
--       ((K₀ * dP6 P n * (zsz (pP6 P n : ℤ) + 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) ≤
--         (KP6 P n : ℝ) * (dP6 P n : ℝ) ^ P.lamp
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language (I3): the extra hypotheses of `P14NeedH'` at round-six parameters
--
--   `p14_hyps_r6`: for `P.Ok`, any constant `K₀` and all large `n`, the round-six values
--   `K = KP6 = ℓ - 1`, `D = dP6 = ⌊b^ε⌋`, `p = pP6 = 6 b^(1+x)` satisfy
--
--   1. `zsz N ≤ p` for every `N < 2^(6b)` (and `n ≤ 2^b`, `V ≤ 48 n`, so every local size of the
--      caller is far below);
--   2. `(p + K₀)^5 ≤ 2^K`;
--   3. `K₀ D (zsz p + 1) ≤ K D^lamp` (this is `ε (2 - lamp) < 1`, `Prm.Ok.eps_two_sub`);
--
--   and also `6 ≤ K`.
--
